---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/href';
import Widget from '../../components/InputDecoupling.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Manipulated Input Decoupling — ECE/ME 732">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={href("/interactives/")}>← Interactives</a></p>
  <h1>Manipulated Input Decoupling</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Actuators are mounted where there is room for them, which is rarely where
    the states are. Two actuators either side of a body each push it and turn
    it, so a command to one of them is a command to both states at once.
    Invert the geometry in the controller and each command reaches one state.
    The test is a null test: command one state and look for the other to stay
    at exactly zero.
  </p>
  <Widget />
</BaseLayout>
